'''Dicranaceae''' is a family of [[Peristome#In mosses|haplolepideous]] [[moss]]es ([[Dicranidae]]) in class [[Bryopsida]]. Species within this family are [[dioicous]].<ref>{{cite journal |last=Williams |first=R. S. |year=1913 |title=Dicranaceae |series=North American Flora | publisher=New York Botanical Garden | volume=15 | issue=1–2 }}</ref> Genera in this family include ''[[Dicranum]]'', ''[[Dicranoloma]]'', and ''[[Mitrobryum]]''.

